<% content_for :title, "Quotes | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="perspectives-quotes-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="perspectives-quotes-hero">

    <div class="perspectives-quotes-hero-content">

      <p class="perspectives-quotes-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / PERSPECTIVES / QUOTES
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>WORDS</span>
        <span>WORTH</span>
        <span>KEEPING.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="perspectives-quotes-intro">
        SHIT I UNDERLINED.<br>
        SHIT I WROTE DOWN.<br>
        SHIT THAT FOLLOWED ME HOME.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="pq-section pq-section-black">

    <p class="pq-number">01 / WHY QUOTES?</p>

    <h2>
      SOMETIMES<br>
      ONE FUCKING<br>
      SENTENCE.
    </h2>

    <div class="pq-copy">

      <p>
        I like quotes because sometimes somebody manages to put
        an entire idea into one sentence.
      </p>

      <p>
        But I'm not interested in collecting profound-looking words
        just because they'd look good slapped over a sunset.
      </p>

      <p>
        If I keep a quote, I want to know why.
      </p>

      <div class="pq-callout">
        WHAT DID IT MAKE ME NOTICE?<br>
        WHAT DID IT CHALLENGE?<br>
        WHY THE FUCK DID I SAVE IT?
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- QUOTES -->
  <section class="pq-library">

    <div class="pq-library-heading">

      <p>02 / THE COLLECTION</p>

      <h2>
        READ IT.<br>
        SIT WITH IT.<br>
        ARGUE WITH IT.
      </h2>

      <p>
        A growing collection of words that made me stop
        long enough to think.
      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="pq-grid">


      <!-- QUOTE 01 -->
      <article class="pq-card pq-card-pink">

        <p class="pq-card-number">01</p>

        <blockquote>
          “YOUR QUOTE GOES HERE.”
        </blockquote>

        <p class="pq-source">
          — AUTHOR / SOURCE
        </p>

        <div class="pq-reflection">

          <span>WHY I KEPT IT</span>

          <p>
            This is where I write what the quote actually means
            to me instead of letting somebody else's words
            do all the fucking work.
          </p>

        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- QUOTE 02 -->
      <article class="pq-card pq-card-yellow">

        <p class="pq-card-number">02</p>

        <blockquote>
          “YOUR QUOTE GOES HERE.”
        </blockquote>

        <p class="pq-source">
          — AUTHOR / SOURCE
        </p>

        <div class="pq-reflection">

          <span>WHY I KEPT IT</span>

          <p>
            What was happening when I found it?
            What did it remind me of?
            What part of my life did it hit?
          </p>

        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- QUOTE 03 -->
      <article class="pq-card pq-card-purple">

        <p class="pq-card-number">03</p>

        <blockquote>
          “YOUR QUOTE GOES HERE.”
        </blockquote>

        <p class="pq-source">
          — AUTHOR / SOURCE
        </p>

        <div class="pq-reflection">

          <span>WHY I KEPT IT</span>

          <p>
            Maybe I agree with it.
            Maybe I don't completely.
            Maybe that's exactly why I wrote the fucking thing down.
          </p>

        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- QUOTE 04 -->
      <article class="pq-card pq-card-black">

        <p class="pq-card-number">04</p>

        <blockquote>
          “YOUR QUOTE GOES HERE.”
        </blockquote>

        <p class="pq-source">
          — AUTHOR / SOURCE
        </p>

        <div class="pq-reflection">

          <span>WHY I KEPT IT</span>

          <p>
            The part that stayed with me after I closed the book,
            left the room, or moved on with my day.
          </p>

        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- QUOTE 05 -->
      <article class="pq-card pq-card-yellow">

        <p class="pq-card-number">05</p>

        <blockquote>
          “YOUR QUOTE GOES HERE.”
        </blockquote>

        <p class="pq-source">
          — AUTHOR / SOURCE
        </p>

        <div class="pq-reflection">

          <span>WHY I KEPT IT</span>

          <p>
            Some words don't give me an answer.
            They just give me a better fucking question.
          </p>

        </div>

      </article>


      <!-- QUOTE 06 -->
      <article class="pq-card pq-card-pink">

        <p class="pq-card-number">06</p>

        <blockquote>
          “YOUR QUOTE GOES HERE.”
        </blockquote>

        <p class="pq-source">
          — AUTHOR / SOURCE
        </p>

        <div class="pq-reflection">

          <span>WHY I KEPT IT</span>

          <p>
            If it changed the way I looked at something,
            it earns a place here.
          </p>

        </div>

      </article>


    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CATEGORIES -->
  <section class="pq-section pq-section-yellow">

    <p class="pq-number">03 / WHAT I KEEP COMING BACK TO</p>

    <h2>
      SAME QUESTIONS.<br>
      DIFFERENT<br>
      WORDS.
    </h2>

    <div class="pq-copy">

      <p>
        The quotes I save tend to circle around the same handful
        of things.
      </p>

      <div class="pq-tags">

        <span>RECOVERY</span>
        <span>ADDICTION</span>
        <span>SUFFERING</span>
        <span>IMPERMANENCE</span>
        <span>ANGER</span>
        <span>FORGIVENESS</span>
        <span>IDENTITY</span>
        <span>COURAGE</span>
        <span>SHAME</span>
        <span>GRIEF</span>
        <span>CHANGE</span>
        <span>FREEDOM</span>
        <span>COMPASSION</span>
        <span>MENTAL HEALTH</span>
        <span>STARTING OVER</span>

      </div>

      <p>
        Apparently my brain has themes.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CONTEXT -->
  <section class="pq-section pq-section-purple">

    <p class="pq-number">04 / CONTEXT MATTERS</p>

    <h2>
      TEN WORDS<br>
      AREN'T THE<br>
      WHOLE BOOK.
    </h2>

    <div class="pq-copy">

      <p>
        A quote is a fragment.
      </p>

      <p>
        It can be useful, beautiful, funny, uncomfortable,
        or exactly what I needed to read that day.
      </p>

      <p>
        It can also lose half its meaning when somebody rips it
        away from everything surrounding it.
      </p>

      <div class="pq-thought">
        WHO SAID IT?<br>
        WHERE DID IT COME FROM?<br>
        WHAT WERE THEY ACTUALLY TALKING ABOUT?
      </div>

      <p>
        Context doesn't ruin a good quote.
      </p>

      <p>
        Usually it makes the quote more fucking interesting.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- MY WORDS -->
  <section class="pq-section pq-section-pink">

    <p class="pq-number">05 / AND SOMETIMES IT'S MINE</p>

    <h2>
      WRITE YOUR<br>
      OWN SHIT<br>
      DOWN.
    </h2>

    <div class="pq-copy">

      <p>
        Not everything worth remembering came from somebody famous.
      </p>

      <p>
        Sometimes it's something I wrote in a journal.
        Something somebody said to me.
        Something I realized in recovery.
        Something I scribbled down because I knew I'd forget it later.
      </p>

      <p>
        Those belong here too.
      </p>

      <div class="pq-callout">
        YOUR OWN WORDS DON'T HAVE TO BE<br>
        FAMOUS TO BE WORTH REMEMBERING.
      </div>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- ENDING -->
  <section class="pq-ending">

    <p>
      DON'T JUST SAVE THE WORDS.
    </p>

    <h2>
      ASK WHY<br>
      THEY FUCKING<br>
      MATTER.
    </h2>

    <p class="pq-ending-copy">
      Keep the ones that make you stop.
      Keep the ones that make you think.
      Keep the ones you need to find again.
    </p>

    <%= link_to "← BACK TO PERSPECTIVES",
        perspectives_path,
        class: "pq-back-link" %>

  </section>

</main>